<td id="S4.T1.2.1.5.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.5.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.9999</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Dimension Contribution: Participation Ratio</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To quantify how many dimensions effectively contribute, we compute the <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">participation ratio</span> (PR) on absolute magnitudes <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=|c_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=|c_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\mathrm{PR}(v)=\frac{\big(\sum_{i=1}^{d}v_{i}\big)^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{d}v_{i}^{2}},\quad\alpha_{\text{norm}}=\frac{\alpha}{d}\ \text{, with d is dimension}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>PR</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>norm</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>, with d is dimension</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\mathrm{PR}(v)=\frac{\big(\sum_{i=1}^{d}v_{i}\big)^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{d}v_{i}^{2}},\quad\alpha_{\text{norm}}=\frac{\alpha}{d}\ \text{, with d is dimension}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">PR estimates the number of coordinates carrying most of the total magnitude. Tab. <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 Magnitude Histograms ‣ 4 Emergent Property II: Sparse Magnitude Distribution ‣ A Hidden Semantic Bottleneck in Conditional Embeddings of Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows that state-of-the-art models (MDT, LightningDiT, MG, REPA) rely on less than 2% of dimensions, whereas continuous tasks such as X-MDPT and MDSGen use a larger fraction (13–48%) and exhibit even higher cosine similarity (up to 99.99% vs. 90–99.4%).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This suggests that continuous-condition embeddings both engage more dimensions and distribute information more uniformly, naturally leading to stronger alignment across samples compared to discrete class-conditional ImageNet generation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F7" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:60%;"><img src="2602.21596v1/head_removed2.png" id="S4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:329/138;" width="329" height="138" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>
<span id="S4.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Class-conditioned image generation with head removal.</span> ImageNet samples after pruning top-magnitude dimensions of <math id="S4.F7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{c}</annotation></semantics></math> (threshold <math id="S4.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>); removing only a few head dimensions markedly degrades quality. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>From Observation to Action: Pruning Redundant Dimensions</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Role of tail dimensions.</span>
To quantify sparsity and effective dimensionality, we define the <span id="S5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">sparsity ratio</span> at threshold <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S5.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{tail}(\tau)}=\frac{1}{d}\#\{i:\,|c_{i}|&lt;\tau\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mtext>tail</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{tail}(\tau)}=\frac{1}{d}\#\{i:\,|c_{i}|&lt;\tau\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">With <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe a sparsity ratio of <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\approx 0.38" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.38</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\approx 0.38</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.40</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the high-magnitude “head” as
<math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{head}}(\tau)=\frac{1}{d}\#\{i:|c_{i}|&gt;\tau\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>head</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{head}}(\tau)=\frac{1}{d}\#\{i:|c_{i}|&gt;\tau\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the low-magnitude “tail” as the remaining coordinates. Using REPA as a representative model, we progressively prune <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{c}</annotation></semantics></math> at thresholds <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\{0.01,0.02,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.02</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\{0.01,0.02,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math> and find that FID and CLIP scores remain stable–even after removing up to 66% of dimensions (Tab. <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5 From Observation to Action: Pruning Redundant Dimensions ‣ A Hidden Semantic Bottleneck in Conditional Embeddings of Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), showing substantial redundancy.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table" style="width:60%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Performance and semantic metrics under sparsification. <math id="S5.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>: prune every step, <math id="S5.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>: prune only at start, <math id="S5.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n-k,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n-k,n}</annotation></semantics></math>: prune during last <math id="S5.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> steps.</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:238.5pt;height:75pt;vertical-align:-36.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-75.4pt,23.7pt) scale(0.612512568243352,0.612512568243352) ;">
<table id="S5.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S5.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S5.T2.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:6.8pt;height:26.3pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:26.3pt;transform:translate(-9.7pt,-9.7pt) rotate(-90deg) ;">
<span id="S5.T2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Prune</span>
</span></span></span></th>
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Threshold <math id="S5.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"># Removed Dims</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FID ↓</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">IS ↑</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">CLIP</span><span id="S5.T2.2.1.1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">↑</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Baseline (REPA)</td>
